e called pre-flop and flop with.\n\n**Reason:**\n\nChecking is the optimal play here. My two pair (10s and 3s) is vulnerable to overcards. The opponent's turn check suggests they don't have a monster, but they could easily have an Ace, Queen, or Jack that beats me. By checking:\n- I control the pot size with a marginal hand\n- I avoid getting raised off a hand that might be ahead\n- I can still win at showdown if they also check\n- If they bet, I can fold against aggression\n\nThis is a way-ahead-or-way-behind scenario, and checking allows me to realize my equity without unnecessary risk while protecting my chip lead.\n\n**Answer:** 0"}
